# Loaded by `vite build` (npm run build) — the worldsoccersim.org build.
#
# Committed on purpose. Vite inlines `import.meta.env.VITE_*` at build time, so
# these have to exist wherever the build runs, and every place that could hold
# them out-of-band is a place they can be silently lost: they lived in the
# Vercel project, the 2026-08-15 move to Cloudflare left them behind, and
# production shipped a bundle carrying `posthog.init(undefined)` for five days.
# Nothing throws and nothing logs when that happens — the site just reports no
# pageviews, no gameplay events and no crashes while looking perfectly healthy.
#
# Keeping the values in the repo means any checkout builds a working bundle
# with no dashboard configuration anywhere, which is the only version of this
# that cannot be lost again in a host migration.
#
# Safe to commit: VITE_POSTHOG_KEY is PostHog's public project API key. It is
# write-only, and it is already served to every visitor inside the JS bundle.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_nqhYqPRCqWKbvbmWV4Nqs4NzmVP2xA8fUgtAMdGnF9FZ

# The US ingestion endpoint, not the app URL (us.posthog.com).
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
